A1. A wise remark. ~ CRACK
A6. A stop signal. ~ SMACK
A11. A shoe clerk on his holidays. ~ SHEIK
A13. Girl friend of the above mentioned clerk. ~ SHEBA
A15. Adeline Moore (Careful now!). ~ PS
A17. Prefix meaning against. ~ ANTI
A18. What men do if they argue with their wives. ~ LOSE
A19. Point of the compass. ~ SE
A20. Impersonal possessive pronoun. ~ ITS
A22. These are usually hanging around the women. ~ TEDDIES
A24. Department of Public Cheeses (init.). ~ DPC
A25. Where Chicagoans get knocked for a loop. ~ LOOP
A27. Nefarious Artichoke Dunkers (init.). ~ NAD
A28. Jack Dempsey's wax model. ~ BEAK
A29. This is worth about two cents in Chicago. ~ LIFE
A30. Satan's sanctum sanctorum. ~ HADES
A32. Wild grains. ~ OATS
A33. This is a lot of tomato sauce! ~ CATSUP
A35. Spanish gentlemen. ~ SENORS
